## What changed (by symbol)

F1 — release authorization (Major, security / CWE-862)
  packages/mpd-team-core-plugin/src/team-store.ts
    + authorizeRelease(record, taskId, caller, lead): string | undefined
        allowed: this team's LEAD (roster flag OR the record's own leadSessionId/leadHistory)
                 or the task's OWNER (private nameMatches, the close gate's comparator)
        refused: a stranger -> the close gate's own sentence
                 no owner     -> "task X has no owner and this caller is not this team's lead"
                 task gone    -> only the Lead may free the stale pairing
  packages/mpd-team-core-plugin/src/index.ts
    ~ releaseDispatchedTask(..., caller, lead): the record is re-read FIRST and authorizeRelease
      runs at the TOP, BEFORE the ledger write — an unauthorized caller unbooks nothing.
    ~ agent_teams_task release: caller = [sessionId, sessionTitleOf(exec), membership name,
      ownMember.name, narrowed ancestry]; lead = membership?.role === "lead" (the close branch's
      own sources; `claimant` is never read).
    ~ agent_teams_dispatch release: the SAME construction and the SAME lead source.

F2 — release render (Minor)
  packages/mpd-team-core-plugin/src/index.ts  agent_teams_task output.render
    `released` is now checked BEFORE `status` (after `refused`):
      released true                     -> `${taskId} -> ${status ?? "pending"} (pairing freed)`
      released false, status present    -> `${taskId} -> ${status} (no pairing to free)`
      released false, no status         -> "that task was not dispatched"
    The close line is unchanged and no schema changed; the dispatch render is untouched.

F3 — settled member claim (Minor, state)
  packages/mpd-team-core-plugin/src/index.ts  agent_teams_task claim
    memberNamedBy(claimed, [claimant]) resolves the claimant's roster row; when it is `inactive`
    the written record is withDerivedPhase(updateTeamMember(..., {status:"running"})).
    `failed` / `provisioning` rows are left alone; the phase is re-derived either way.

Docs
  packages/mpd-team-core-plugin/README.md + README.zh-CN.md — who may release (the Lead or the
  task's own owner) and that an unauthorized release is refused BEFORE the pairing is freed (EN/zh
  in lockstep).

