## Bounds

- A non-Lead release of a task id that is NO LONGER on the board is refused and no longer frees a
  stale ledger pairing; the Lead keeps that repair and the dispatch pass's own reconcile prunes
  such rows. Deliberate under the "Lead or owner" rule, documented in authorizeRelease.
- The caller-identity array is copied from the close branch instead of being extracted (the
  contract forbade inventing helpers); it now appears in three places.
- Authorization decides against the record re-read at the top of releaseDispatchedTask; the ledger
  write follows it. A concurrent owner change is still bounded by casReleaseTask's revision CAS,
  but the authorization itself is not revision-fenced.
- Gates ran on the wave's own DIRTY tree (pre-commit, as intended). An earlier capture recorded a
  non-zero exit before any log existed: a command substitution on the per-call fresh /tmp failed,
  short-circuiting `&&` so the gate never ran. Re-run directly, captured cleanly here; the package
  suite was also run five consecutive times, all 280 pass / exit 0.
